From f7a335ffc54f2356ed20bc5920ee6a8c7211d5b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:03:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] MSL: Transform feedback in emulated geometry shaders

Transform feedback of a geometry shader (zink with a geometry shader on every draw, DXVK's
stream-output geometry shaders) did not compile: one 'int gl_VertexIndex = 0' per captured
output, the buffer declared const, and every vertex written at index 0 regardless of the
output topology. Stream-output-only geometry shaders without a position also did not compile
('missing mesh output declaration with attribute position').

- Geometry shaders without a position output get an implicit one: the vertices of a Metal
  mesh need it.
- Captured outputs are written by the mesh stream when an output primitive is complete,
  decomposed into points, lines or triangles in the order of the output topology (odd strip
  triangles as (t, t + 2, t + 1)), to up to 4 buffers at Offset within XfbStride, skipping
  buffers that are not bound.
- The vertices of a draw must be written in primitive order, but each input primitive emits a
  varying number of vertices. The mesh entry point therefore runs in two modes: 1 counts the
  captured vertices of each input primitive (and outputs no primitives), 2 writes them at the
  first vertex slot of the primitive computed by the API from the counts. Options
  xfb_buffer_index (buffer b at xfb_buffer_index - b), xfb_session_index (sizes, offsets,
  strides, used buffers), xfb_prims_index (per-primitive counts/slots), xfb_mode_index.
- The object stage passes the input primitive index over all instances in the payload.
- OpEmitStreamVertex / OpEndStreamPrimitive of stream 0 emit; other streams are ignored.
- Rasterized strip triangles also use the (t, t + 2, t + 1) order for odd triangles (front
  faces of odd strip triangles were reversed).
- Remove a debug printf of the transform feedback buffer id.
